  "text": "Garcroft Supply\n\nThree facts about lighthouses:\n1. Lighthouses use powerful lenses, such as Fresnel lenses, to project light over long distances.\n2. The color of a lighthouse's light and its flash pattern are unique to each location, helping mariners identify their position.\n3. Early lighthouses often used burning materials like wood or coal, which were later replaced by oil, electricity, and eventually solar power.\n\nGUGUWI-HEXINU"
